# QR Guard roadmap

## Phase 1: MVP foundation

- [ ] Create repository structure and initial backend scaffold
- [ ] Implement URL normalization and risk classification engine
- [ ] Add HTTP API to classify URLs before opening them
- [ ] Build smart contract skeleton for reputation records
- [ ] Document architecture and threat model

## Phase 2: Threat intelligence integration

- [ ] Add adapters for Google Safe Browsing, OpenPhish, PhishTank, and URLhaus
- [ ] Cache threat intelligence results using Redis
- [ ] Add domain reputation scoring from historical data and reports
- [ ] Add false-positive and false-negative reporting support

## Phase 3: QR code experience

- [ ] Build QR camera scan flow
- [ ] Extract URLs and detect malicious destination before open
- [ ] Show clear risk warnings: safe / suspicious / malicious
- [ ] Add allowlist support for trusted domains
- [ ] Support file-based QR code ingestion for testing

## Phase 4: Blockchain layer

- [ ] Add governance model for report validation
- [ ] Introduce staking for reporters and validators
- [ ] Add transparent deploy flow for network selection
- [ ] Store hashed URL data and report attestations on-chain
- [ ] Automatically reconcile on-chain scores with backend reputation data

## Phase 5: Production hardening

- [ ] Add rate limiting, abuse protection, and anti-Sybil safeguards
- [ ] Add privacy controls and data minimization checks
- [ ] Run security audits on smart contracts and app logic
- [ ] Add telemetry and risk dashboards
- [ ] Support multiple mobile platforms and secure update channels

## Success metrics

- 95%+ detection rate for known phishing payloads
- low false-positive rate on trusted domains
- user warning latency under 2 seconds for common checks
- on-chain reputation updates validated across multiple reporter submissions

## Recommended next milestone

The next implementation milestone is building the backend classification API and integrating a live threat feed adapter, then adding the QR scanning UI and blockchain reporting workflow.
